(4444627, 639031, 18374, '<td valign="top">This looks a bit overexposed and oversaturated to me.  Perhaps you monitor is set too dark?</td>', 'This looks a bit overexposed and oversaturated to me.  Perhaps you monitor is set too dark?', '2008-01-31 21:36:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444628, 638267, 18374, '<td valign="top">Very nice.  I love the detail in the eye.</td>', 'Very nice.  I love the detail in the eye.', '2008-01-31 21:39:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444641, 638777, 83313, '<td valign="top">Lots of good detail here, and an interesting bird for sure. Not thrilling me, however. Maybe it''s the near solid dark background, or the crop, but I''m not sure.</td>', 'Lots of good detail here, and an interesting bird for sure. Not thrilling me, however. Maybe it''s the near solid dark background, or the crop, but I''m not sure.', '2008-01-31 21:51:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444653, 637342, 83313, '<td valign="top">Your file size is only 51k when you could have used up to 200k. This indicates a lot of JPEG compression, which is surely taking a lot of detail out of your photo. Check the JPEG compression settings in your image editor and always try to save as close to the limit for a challenge as you can get it without going over.</td>', 'Your file size is only 51k when you could have used up to 200k. This indicates a lot of JPEG compression, which is surely taking a lot of detail out of your photo. Check the JPEG compression settings in your image editor and always try to save as close to the limit for a challenge as you can get it without going over.', '2008-01-31 21:55:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444654, 639057, 83313, '<td valign="top">Your file size is only 51k when you could have used up to 200k. This indicates a lot of JPEG compression, which is taking a lot of detail out of your photo. Check the JPEG compression settings in your image editor and always try to save as close to the limit for a challenge as you can get it without going over.<br/> <br/>This shot also looks a bit overprocessed on the birds body. I can''t tell for sure what may have caused this.</td>', 'Your file size is only 51k when you could have used up to 200k. This indicates a lot of JPEG compression, which is taking a lot of detail out of your photo. Check the JPEG compression settings in your image editor and always try to save as close to the limit for a challenge as you can get it without going over. This shot also looks a bit overprocessed on the birds body. I can''t tell for sure what may have caused this.', '2008-01-31 21:58:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444657, 638922, 83313, '<td valign="top">I''m not fond of the reflection in the glass, it distracts from the subject of the bird. I do see some good effort to compose and crop the shot well.</td>', 'I''m not fond of the reflection in the glass, it distracts from the subject of the bird. I do see some good effort to compose and crop the shot well.', '2008-01-31 22:01:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444661, 639014, 83313, '<td valign="top">What great detail showing on this little guy! I''m not fond of the amount of empty space you left in the frame, but that''s more of a preference on my part than a fault of your entry.</td>', 'What great detail showing on this little guy! I''m not fond of the amount of empty space you left in the frame, but that''s more of a preference on my part than a fault of your entry.', '2008-01-31 22:03:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444667, 638130, 62249, '<td valign="top">This shot has tremendous potential, but there''s an odd smoothness to the swan that doesn''t look right. Still, the graphic quality of the black reflections in the water is quite nice.</td>', 'This shot has tremendous potential, but there''s an odd smoothness to the swan that doesn''t look right. Still, the graphic quality of the black reflections in the water is quite nice.', '2008-01-31 22:05:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444668, 638876, 83313, '<td valign="top">Great in flight catch. Judging from the blur on the bird in the water, you were probably panning to get this. What a catch!</td>', 'Great in flight catch. Judging from the blur on the bird in the water, you were probably panning to get this. What a catch!', '2008-01-31 22:06:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444670, 638975, 62249, '<td valign="top">Try a tighter crop to fill more of the frame with the bird and reflection. Lighting on the bird is nice.</td>', 'Try a tighter crop to fill more of the frame with the bird and reflection. Lighting on the bird is nice.', '2008-01-31 22:06:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444672, 638637, 83313, '<td valign="top">Nice enough except for the schmutz on his beak. I think the comp may have worked a bit better with a bit more space on the right of the frame.</td>', 'Nice enough except for the schmutz on his beak. I think the comp may have worked a bit better with a bit more space on the right of the frame.', '2008-01-31 22:07:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444678, 637603, 83313, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous bird. I think it could have used a little more saturation or contrast to do it justice. <br/> <br/>Also, your file size is a lot smaller than was allowed. You may have lost some clarity to JPEg compression. Check the JPEG compression settings in your image editor and always try to save as close to the limit for a challenge as you can get it without going over.</td>', 'Gorgeous bird. I think it could have used a little more saturation or contrast to do it justice.  Also, your file size is a lot smaller than was allowed. You may have lost some clarity to JPEg compression. Check the JPEG compression settings in your image editor and always try to save as close to the limit for a challenge as you can get it without going over.', '2008-01-31 22:10:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444684, 638788, 83313, '<td valign="top">Neat looking. Only critique I have offhand is the fact that his head is hidden in shadows. Wild animals don''t exactly pose for you.</td>', 'Neat looking. Only critique I have offhand is the fact that his head is hidden in shadows. Wild animals don''t exactly pose for you.', '2008-01-31 22:12:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444688, 638905, 83313, '<td valign="top">And the ladies are ignoring him... <br/> <br/>Good punchy colors, but not overdone.</td>', 'And the ladies are ignoring him...  Good punchy colors, but not overdone.', '2008-01-31 22:13:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444694, 638286, 83313, '<td valign="top">The bird is almost lost in the similar surrounding colors.</td>', 'The bird is almost lost in the similar surrounding colors.', '2008-01-31 22:15:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444701, 638826, 83313, '<td valign="top">Cute bird, but there seems to be a lack of detail here, and the contrast could use a bump up. I''ll bet a quick tweak with curves would punch this up nicely.</td>', 'Cute bird, but there seems to be a lack of detail here, and the contrast could use a bump up. I''ll bet a quick tweak with curves would punch this up nicely.', '2008-01-31 22:17:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444709, 638415, 83313, '<td valign="top">Why does this guy remind me of Big Bird? Love the detail and the orange eye. Punched up, but not overdone. Actually, come the think of it, I''m faving this one.</td>', 'Why does this guy remind me of Big Bird? Love the detail and the orange eye. Punched up, but not overdone. Actually, come the think of it, I''m faving this one.', '2008-01-31 22:19:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444735, 638986, 1054, '<td valign="top">From a technical standpoint, the tack-sharp panning on the right skate is quite impressive, so kudos on that accomplishment.<br/> <br/>I''m torn on how to rate this. One the one hand, it''s quite a good photo. On the other, it doesn''t strictly meet the definition of the challenge, and though the title makes the connection, this is a <i>photo</i> contest, not a <i>title</i> contest.<br/> <br/>The girl''s pose is more reminiscent of a runner than a bird... if the left arm was more fully outstretched, you might have me on that. Ordinaly I halve the score for a DNMC entry. I''m going to do that here, but add back a point for making me think outside the box, ending up at 5. Had you saved this for the Free Study, you would have received an 8 from me.</td>', 'From a technical standpoint, the tack-sharp panning on the right skate is quite impressive, so kudos on that accomplishment. I''m torn on how to rate this. One the one hand, it''s quite a good photo. On the other, it doesn''t strictly meet the definition of the challenge, and though the title makes the connection, this is a photo contest, not a title contest. The girl''s pose is more reminiscent of a runner than a bird... if the left arm was more fully outstretched, you might have me on that. Ordinaly I halve the score for a DNMC entry. I''m going to do that here, but add back a point for making me think outside the box, ending up at 5. Had you saved this for the Free Study, you would have received an 8 from me.', '2008-01-31 22:26:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444796, 638666, 62249, '<td valign="top">Work on better focus. Also, back of bird is too shadowed.</td>', 'Work on better focus. Also, back of bird is too shadowed.', '2008-01-31 22:42:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444801, 638709, 62249, '<td valign="top">Nicely composed. Seems oversharpened.</td>', 'Nicely composed. Seems oversharpened.', '2008-01-31 22:45:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444804, 638995, 61577, '<td valign="top">Great shot very crisp... Love the addition of the twig</td>', 'Great shot very crisp... Love the addition of the twig', '2008-01-31 22:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444805, 638723, 62249, '<td valign="top">Consider trying this with different, rather extreme crop. Cut off the upper portion of the photo just above the group of lily pads with the solo purple blossom. This would result in a narrow, horizontal look that would emphasize the "runway" on the water.</td>', 'Consider trying this with different, rather extreme crop. Cut off the upper portion of the photo just above the group of lily pads with the solo purple blossom. This would result in a narrow, horizontal look that would emphasize the "runway" on the water.', '2008-01-31 22:48:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(4444839, 638924, 36619, '<td valign="top">beautiful!</td>', 'beautiful!', '2008-01-31 23:13:06.000000', NULL, 1),
