(4456077, 638032, 66384, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BrianR:</b></div><hr/><i> My reason for a little soft in the focus, is the texture is lost on the breast of the bird. and how did you get an aperture of 1.8 on a lens that reads 3.5 ? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks for catching the mistake, Brian. I have corrected the lens in the image info. I was using a 50mm f1.4 prime lens.</td>', 'Originally posted by BrianR: My reason for a little soft in the focus, is the texture is lost on the breast of the bird. and how did you get an aperture of 1.8 on a lens that reads 3.5 ?  Thanks for catching the mistake, Brian. I have corrected the lens in the image info. I was using a 50mm f1.4 prime lens.', '2008-02-04 01:23:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4456086, 638925, 39184, '<td valign="top">Wow!  You really blew away your previous PB.  This is one of the shots that I went looking for after the challenge to see how well it did.  The focus on those colors is perfect.  Great job.</td>', 'Wow!  You really blew away your previous PB.  This is one of the shots that I went looking for after the challenge to see how well it did.  The focus on those colors is perfect.  Great job.', '2008-02-04 01:32:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4456091, 638803, 68035, '<td valign="top">Well, your post voting comments mades me laugh...good advice which I would do well to remember myself on occasion.<br/> <br/>I guess its reassuring for someone like me to know that even great photographers can have their off shots.  The funny thing is that this is nearly a great shot, I loved the suspended water coming off the ducks body.  Strangely I actually prefer it on some levels to your outtake, which although technically is a better shot and I am sure would have scored higher feels like a very safe option, this however was an image that felt a lot more challenging<br/> <br/></td>', 'Well, your post voting comments mades me laugh...good advice which I would do well to remember myself on occasion. I guess its reassuring for someone like me to know that even great photographers can have their off shots.  The funny thing is that this is nearly a great shot, I loved the suspended water coming off the ducks body.  Strangely I actually prefer it on some levels to your outtake, which although technically is a better shot and I am sure would have scored higher feels like a very safe option, this however was an image that felt a lot more challenging ', '2008-02-04 01:37:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4456099, 637912, 68035, '<td valign="top">Cracking shot Karen that got an 8 from me although I am surprised you have pigeons (winged rats) in Nfld as I thought they were generally city birds.  I loved the tight crop, the sharpness and of course the range of colours which had a real electric feel to them.  Very impressive finish in what I thought was a challenge which had a lot of outstanding images in it<br/> <br/></td>', 'Cracking shot Karen that got an 8 from me although I am surprised you have pigeons (winged rats) in Nfld as I thought they were generally city birds.  I loved the tight crop, the sharpness and of course the range of colours which had a real electric feel to them.  Very impressive finish in what I thought was a challenge which had a lot of outstanding images in it ', '2008-02-04 01:41:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4456100, 637977, 39184, '<td valign="top">Good sharpness that is not overdone as happens often.  I like the plain black background and how it sets off the color.  Congratulations on a new personal best.</td>', 'Good sharpness that is not overdone as happens often.  I like the plain black background and how it sets off the color.  Congratulations on a new personal best.', '2008-02-04 01:42:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4456103, 638274, 68035, '<td valign="top">This was a really nice shot for the challenge simply because it was so different to the vast majority of images.<br/> <br/>I thought the composition was fantastic, espially the way you captured the melting ice were the goose had walked.  Really strong black and whire conversion as well.  Mind you just looking at that wing made me wince</td>', 'This was a really nice shot for the challenge simply because it was so different to the vast majority of images. I thought the composition was fantastic, espially the way you captured the melting ice were the goose had walked.  Really strong black and whire conversion as well.  Mind you just looking at that wing made me wince', '2008-02-04 01:46:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4456108, 637288, 68035, '<td valign="top">I see some experimentation went on here!!!  (for me it kinda worked - I gave it a 6).  I had loved the composition and the detail of the lead bird, but (IMO) it had a little too much contrast which when combined with the high key meant that it almost had a collage like appearance (some of e301''s stuff has that ethereal ''appearing from the light'' quality)<br/> <br/>One that stood out from the crowd in terms of the way that the challenge had been interpreted and all the better for that</td>', 'I see some experimentation went on here!!!  (for me it kinda worked - I gave it a 6).  I had loved the composition and the detail of the lead bird, but (IMO) it had a little too much contrast which when combined with the high key meant that it almost had a collage like appearance (some of e301''s stuff has that ethereal ''appearing from the light'' quality) One that stood out from the crowd in terms of the way that the challenge had been interpreted and all the better for that', '2008-02-04 01:53:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4456111, 636550, 39184, '<td valign="top">Nice work getting a clean background.  Great detail throughout most of the white which is very difficult to accomplish.  The detail also in the eye that is most visible to us.  I bet this looks even more fantastic in print.</td>', 'Nice work getting a clean background.  Great detail throughout most of the white which is very difficult to accomplish.  The detail also in the eye that is most visible to us.  I bet this looks even more fantastic in print.', '2008-02-04 01:56:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4456117, 638855, 68035, '<td valign="top">The title of this image had made me smile during voting as it seemed to capture the ''expression'' on the swam perfectly.  Beautiful composition (talk about a cool ''s-curve''), lovely detail and thewater has a fantastic soft quality to it.  Great capture of the underbill too whilst still getting the splash of colour from the top of the bill<br/> <br/>I love swans and this is a super shot of one</td>', 'The title of this image had made me smile during voting as it seemed to capture the ''expression'' on the swam perfectly.  Beautiful composition (talk about a cool ''s-curve''), lovely detail and thewater has a fantastic soft quality to it.  Great capture of the underbill too whilst still getting the splash of colour from the top of the bill I love swans and this is a super shot of one', '2008-02-04 01:57:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4456139, 638393, 55956, '<td valign="top">Hi Robert, Congratulations!!!!!!!!!!!</td>', 'Hi Robert, Congratulations!!!!!!!!!!!', '2008-02-04 02:18:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4456152, 637814, 60915, '<td valign="top">I get the funny feeling that he was whistling while he was walking along! : o</td>', 'I get the funny feeling that he was whistling while he was walking along! : o', '2008-02-04 02:38:03.000000', NULL, 0),
