(4457002, 637814, 52115, '<td valign="top">Hi, I''m your neighbor, #133. Just stopped by to say hi.<br/>A sharp, closer view, maybe angled a little more, may have been better. You could ask the bird to stop and pose, but they never listen.</td>', 'Hi, I''m your neighbor, #133. Just stopped by to say hi.A sharp, closer view, maybe angled a little more, may have been better. You could ask the bird to stop and pose, but they never listen.', '2008-02-04 11:09:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457003, 638924, 44877, '<td valign="top">Well, this is certainly underrated - and I''m not just saying that. I love the background, the colors and the composition. The position of the bird is good, too. Stupid voters.</td>', 'Well, this is certainly underrated - and I''m not just saying that. I love the background, the colors and the composition. The position of the bird is good, too. Stupid voters.', '2008-02-04 11:10:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457007, 638916, 18799, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by metatate:</b></div><hr/><i> I have in-laws in Ottumwa Iowa  -I have seen bald eagles flying around there on several occasions so it doesn''t surprise me that this is in Iowa.  I could never even dream of capturing something like this though!  Excellent! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Depending on where and when you go, and the condition of the ice on the Mississippi (mostly frozen with open pockets) you can see literally hundreds of Bald Eagles in one spot.  Depending on the factors, they can be in Ottumwa, Davenport, Burlington or a number of other places - one has to be willing to drive to find them.  By the time the river thaws out they have pretty much dispersed.</td>', 'Originally posted by metatate: I have in-laws in Ottumwa Iowa  -I have seen bald eagles flying around there on several occasions so it doesn''t surprise me that this is in Iowa.  I could never even dream of capturing something like this though!  Excellent!   Depending on where and when you go, and the condition of the ice on the Mississippi (mostly frozen with open pockets) you can see literally hundreds of Bald Eagles in one spot.  Depending on the factors, they can be in Ottumwa, Davenport, Burlington or a number of other places - one has to be willing to drive to find them.  By the time the river thaws out they have pretty much dispersed.', '2008-02-04 11:11:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457010, 638788, 44877, '<td valign="top">Actually, I find the perspective different and refreshing. Not that there''s anything wrong being eye-to-eye with a swan, but this is a twist on the usual swan photos. Love your composition, too.</td>', 'Actually, I find the perspective different and refreshing. Not that there''s anything wrong being eye-to-eye with a swan, but this is a twist on the usual swan photos. Love your composition, too.', '2008-02-04 11:12:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457012, 638129, 42013, '<td valign="top">Really quite funny! Thanks for the match.</td>', 'Really quite funny! Thanks for the match.', '2008-02-04 11:13:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457032, 636505, 52115, '<td valign="top">I like the sharpness of the feathers.<br/>This one is soaring with the eagles.</td>', 'I like the sharpness of the feathers.This one is soaring with the eagles.', '2008-02-04 11:24:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457043, 638664, 84438, '<td valign="top">I like the mention of the Red Yellow and Blue keys to match the ribbon colours.  You might have done better to have mentioned that in the title for a laugh.  But hey, what do I know, I''m right there with you score wise. :)</td>', 'I like the mention of the Red Yellow and Blue keys to match the ribbon colours.  You might have done better to have mentioned that in the title for a laugh.  But hey, what do I know, I''m right there with you score wise. :)', '2008-02-04 11:28:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457055, 638130, 59029, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote in this challenge but I would''ve given this at least a 6.  I like the darkness of the water and shadows surrounding the swan. The soft focus on the swan gives it an ethereal appearance.  However, expecting the vast majority of dpcers to get the meaning behind the pic may be a bit daunting!</td>', 'I didn''t vote in this challenge but I would''ve given this at least a 6.  I like the darkness of the water and shadows surrounding the swan. The soft focus on the swan gives it an ethereal appearance.  However, expecting the vast majority of dpcers to get the meaning behind the pic may be a bit daunting!', '2008-02-04 11:31:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457102, 636450, 11897, '<td valign="top">A beautiful picture and well worthy of the ribbon,<br/>Paul.</td>', 'A beautiful picture and well worthy of the ribbon,Paul.', '2008-02-04 12:03:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457106, 636505, 77192, '<td valign="top">Great shot! Congrats on your top 10. You just scraped over 6 ;-)<br/> <br/>I took a similar shot to this last year (nowhere near as good as yours though) and I''m kicking myself I didn''t think about it when I did my Best of 2007 shot.</td>', 'Great shot! Congrats on your top 10. You just scraped over 6 ;-) I took a similar shot to this last year (nowhere near as good as yours though) and I''m kicking myself I didn''t think about it when I did my Best of 2007 shot.', '2008-02-04 12:06:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457108, 636450, 67152, '<td valign="top">Tim- excellent work again!  Congrats on a ribbon in an extremely strong field of entries</td>', 'Tim- excellent work again!  Congrats on a ribbon in an extremely strong field of entries', '2008-02-04 12:06:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457125, 638820, 83350, '<td valign="top">I still believe this should have gotten a higher score - like we have never seen eagles eating fish (#3). Fantastic soft colors AND great detail!! Great job!!</td>', 'I still believe this should have gotten a higher score - like we have never seen eagles eating fish (#3). Fantastic soft colors AND great detail!! Great job!!', '2008-02-04 12:11:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457150, 638810, 30049, '<td valign="top">New lens, eh?  ;-P  Nice shot!</td>', 'New lens, eh?  ;-P  Nice shot!', '2008-02-04 12:19:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457189, 638655, 66384, '<td valign="top">Karen, I love, love, love this photo. The bokeh is gorgeous and the tree and little nuthatch are in such sharp contrast to the rosy back drop. Don''t you wish the whole world was like that beautiful background?!</td>', 'Karen, I love, love, love this photo. The bokeh is gorgeous and the tree and little nuthatch are in such sharp contrast to the rosy back drop. Don''t you wish the whole world was like that beautiful background?!', '2008-02-04 12:32:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457195, 638306, 50695, '<td valign="top">I gave you a 7. A striking image with cool processing.</td>', 'I gave you a 7. A striking image with cool processing.', '2008-02-04 12:35:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457197, 638682, 66384, '<td valign="top">Nice capture. It looks like water skiing. I like the little laughing gull in the background. Too bad the wing tip is cut off.</td>', 'Nice capture. It looks like water skiing. I like the little laughing gull in the background. Too bad the wing tip is cut off.', '2008-02-04 12:35:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457200, 637478, 67152, '<td valign="top">Catherine - you did an excellent job capturing this gangly and awkward looking birds in flight - what a sight they are to behold</td>', 'Catherine - you did an excellent job capturing this gangly and awkward looking birds in flight - what a sight they are to behold', '2008-02-04 12:38:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457205, 638788, 67152, '<td valign="top">Jon - very well captured image.  The bow of this proud bird to you is a true sign of respect - I am sure there are those that would have liked a bit more face - but I find the lines really quite well captured.</td>', 'Jon - very well captured image.  The bow of this proud bird to you is a true sign of respect - I am sure there are those that would have liked a bit more face - but I find the lines really quite well captured.', '2008-02-04 12:39:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457210, 637478, 66384, '<td valign="top">Beautiful, Catherine. Beautiful birds, beautiful color, beautiful composition, and beautiful moody scene with the fog. Because of the halo along the birds breasts and below their bills, the shot looks a bit over-sharpened. I wonder if it would still be as nice an image with that halo softened a little.</td>', 'Beautiful, Catherine. Beautiful birds, beautiful color, beautiful composition, and beautiful moody scene with the fog. Because of the halo along the birds breasts and below their bills, the shot looks a bit over-sharpened. I wonder if it would still be as nice an image with that halo softened a little.', '2008-02-04 12:40:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457219, 638655, 67152, '<td valign="top">An important tip for you for next time, nuthatches don''t ever stop moving...<br/> <br/>Great image - i love the warm and rich background to contrast the tree and bird - and I think you did an impressive job of it with the shutter speed you had to work with...next time try upping the ISO a bit to allow you a bit faster speeds</td>', 'An important tip for you for next time, nuthatches don''t ever stop moving... Great image - i love the warm and rich background to contrast the tree and bird - and I think you did an impressive job of it with the shutter speed you had to work with...next time try upping the ISO a bit to allow you a bit faster speeds', '2008-02-04 12:43:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457224, 638662, 66384, '<td valign="top">Nice capture of beautiful ducks. I think this might have scored higher if you had cropped it to include just the duck in the foreground. It is nice and sharp with beautiful markings. But, of course, then it wouldn''t have been as interesting an image -- just a pretty bird shot.</td>', 'Nice capture of beautiful ducks. I think this might have scored higher if you had cropped it to include just the duck in the foreground. It is nice and sharp with beautiful markings. But, of course, then it wouldn''t have been as interesting an image -- just a pretty bird shot.', '2008-02-04 12:46:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457225, 639017, 56002, '<td valign="top"><i>Handholding a 400mm lens at 1/20 sec and 1600 ISO</i> <br/> <br/>In the deep south they have an exclamation that I think very appropriate here...<br/> <br/>The hell you say?!</td>', 'Handholding a 400mm lens at 1/20 sec and 1600 ISO  In the deep south they have an exclamation that I think very appropriate here... The hell you say?!', '2008-02-04 12:46:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457230, 637814, 66384, '<td valign="top">This had to be yours. It makes me laugh. I love the composition and the b&amp;w, and the way the bird seems to be marching along with the crowd.</td>', 'This had to be yours. It makes me laugh. I love the composition and the b&w, and the way the bird seems to be marching along with the crowd.', '2008-02-04 12:49:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457243, 638578, 66384, '<td valign="top">Amazing clarity, detail, light, and color. I''m really surprised this didn''t finish in the top ten. Just bad luck that it was such a high scoring challenge.</td>', 'Amazing clarity, detail, light, and color. I''m really surprised this didn''t finish in the top ten. Just bad luck that it was such a high scoring challenge.', '2008-02-04 12:53:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457250, 638991, 66384, '<td valign="top">How cute, you just have to smile when looking at this.</td>', 'How cute, you just have to smile when looking at this.', '2008-02-04 12:56:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457254, 638916, 59267, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on ribbon and PB.</td>', 'Congratulations on ribbon and PB.', '2008-02-04 12:59:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457261, 636450, 59267, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your ribbon!!</td>', 'Congratulations on your ribbon!!', '2008-02-04 13:01:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457262, 637983, 61958, '<td valign="top">So here it is, my critique. Starting with the good; The colours are just great you shot this at a perfect time of day. you''ve processed this very well, with shots like this there is the tempatation to overprocess to make the colours stand out even more you''ve avoinded this and that''s great.<br/> <br/>A couple things I don''t care for much. 1) that border. either a simpler border or none at all would do. the problem with doing too much of a border is it detracts from the photo it self which you never want to do. 2) the branches, to me atleast, make the photo feel very busy. my eye''s don''t know where to look so they look everywhere. maaybe zooming in on a smaller area or (if you have the lens for it) just one bird.<br/> <br/>I didn''t vote in this challenge, but I would have given it a 7<br/> <br/>good job.</td>', 'So here it is, my critique. Starting with the good; The colours are just great you shot this at a perfect time of day. you''ve processed this very well, with shots like this there is the tempatation to overprocess to make the colours stand out even more you''ve avoinded this and that''s great. A couple things I don''t care for much. 1) that border. either a simpler border or none at all would do. the problem with doing too much of a border is it detracts from the photo it self which you never want to do. 2) the branches, to me atleast, make the photo feel very busy. my eye''s don''t know where to look so they look everywhere. maaybe zooming in on a smaller area or (if you have the lens for it) just one bird. I didn''t vote in this challenge, but I would have given it a 7 good job.', '2008-02-04 13:01:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457268, 637288, 66597, '<td valign="top">Peter, you should know better than to enter something artistic here, LOL. I really like this a lot - very Alfred Hitchcock. The only nit is I''m wanting a little more white space on the right side but of course I realize these shots happen so fast that it''s hard to get the composition you want as well as the action. (I assume you added the frame for the purpose of extending that area a bit.) I didn''t vote but would have given you a nice score for artistry.</td>', 'Peter, you should know better than to enter something artistic here, LOL. I really like this a lot - very Alfred Hitchcock. The only nit is I''m wanting a little more white space on the right side but of course I realize these shots happen so fast that it''s hard to get the composition you want as well as the action. (I assume you added the frame for the purpose of extending that area a bit.) I didn''t vote but would have given you a nice score for artistry.', '2008-02-04 13:02:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457271, 638393, 59267, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your blue ribbon!! Excellent shot!</td>', 'Congratulations on your blue ribbon!! Excellent shot!', '2008-02-04 13:03:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457281, 638820, 7473, '<td valign="top">That is quite a colorful bird!  Well captured.</td>', 'That is quite a colorful bird!  Well captured.', '2008-02-04 13:06:44.000000', NULL, 0),
