(4457555, 638130, 60862, '<td valign="top">Jelena, I didn''t vote this challenge, but I would''ve given this a 4 or 5.  I like blur when it''s clearly intentional.  Here, it strikes me as a lack of focus, not intentional use of blur.  That is, I believe you, but I wouldn''t have known that during voting.  I do like the composition.  Now, much more blurred and I might''ve voted higher.  See this shot by Wildcard, for example, which is in my faves:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=565751" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/65000-69999/65035/120/565751.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/65000-69999/65035/120/565751.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/65000-69999/65035/120/565751.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Jelena, I didn''t vote this challenge, but I would''ve given this a 4 or 5.  I like blur when it''s clearly intentional.  Here, it strikes me as a lack of focus, not intentional use of blur.  That is, I believe you, but I wouldn''t have known that during voting.  I do like the composition.  Now, much more blurred and I might''ve voted higher.  See this shot by Wildcard, for example, which is in my faves:', '2008-02-04 14:45:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457563, 638789, 68586, '<td valign="top">Jane - another feathered friend to add to your top line  :- )<br/> <br/>and another nice shot.<br/> <br/>I see you fianlly bought that big white lens then  :- )</td>', 'Jane - another feathered friend to add to your top line  :- ) and another nice shot. I see you fianlly bought that big white lens then  :- )', '2008-02-04 14:47:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457577, 636851, 68586, '<td valign="top">Brad - I''m speechless at where this finished. This was a straight ten for me.<br/> <br/>The string of events that had to come together here for you to get this shot - noticing the shot, getting it despite the weather, getting it despite the lighting under the car, the poignancy of it, the very real battle against nature for this little bird, in an urban setting where his shelter is a car and not a tree . . and of course the capture of the snow drifting across the shot. <br/> <br/>What can I say ? Magnificent.<br/> <br/>Edit for spelling<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-04 15:22:30.</i></td>', 'Brad - I''m speechless at where this finished. This was a straight ten for me. The string of events that had to come together here for you to get this shot - noticing the shot, getting it despite the weather, getting it despite the lighting under the car, the poignancy of it, the very real battle against nature for this little bird, in an urban setting where his shelter is a car and not a tree . . and of course the capture of the snow drifting across the shot.  What can I say ? Magnificent. Edit for spelling', '2008-02-04 14:52:59.000000', '2008-02-04 15:22:30.000000', 0),
(4457578, 639049, 74534, '<td valign="top">Let me add my voice to the people who love this shot - it obviously stands out in the challenge, probably the only image from this challenge that I will remember a month from now. But also it is a great image in its own right, regardless of challenge descriptions and so on. The composition is beautiful, with the lines leading me through the image and making me read it in its entirety before finally resting on the lake and trees. The tones and muted contrast is just fantastic, and the grain contributes to the image as well. Congratulations on a very good shot.</td>', 'Let me add my voice to the people who love this shot - it obviously stands out in the challenge, probably the only image from this challenge that I will remember a month from now. But also it is a great image in its own right, regardless of challenge descriptions and so on. The composition is beautiful, with the lines leading me through the image and making me read it in its entirety before finally resting on the lake and trees. The tones and muted contrast is just fantastic, and the grain contributes to the image as well. Congratulations on a very good shot.', '2008-02-04 14:53:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457585, 639032, 68586, '<td valign="top">I really like the shape and composition here - pity there wasn''t an ''S'' curve challenge going on :- )</td>', 'I really like the shape and composition here - pity there wasn''t an ''S'' curve challenge going on :- )', '2008-02-04 14:56:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457597, 638129, 68586, '<td valign="top">This is a great photo - the DoF is perfect and the cow''s expression is great - perhaps it suffered a little due to the bird not being conspicous enough.<br/> <br/>I know we cant choose these things, but if the bird had been lighter or brighter so it just grabbed the eye a bit more I think this could have gone all the way.<br/> <br/>Still a nice shot.<br/> <br/>edit for dreadful spelling  :- )<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-04 15:20:49.</i></td>', 'This is a great photo - the DoF is perfect and the cow''s expression is great - perhaps it suffered a little due to the bird not being conspicous enough. I know we cant choose these things, but if the bird had been lighter or brighter so it just grabbed the eye a bit more I think this could have gone all the way. Still a nice shot. edit for dreadful spelling  :- )', '2008-02-04 14:59:08.000000', '2008-02-04 15:20:49.000000', 0),
(4457610, 638492, 68586, '<td valign="top">Surely an underrated shot . .<br/> <br/>Barring the winner it seems my thoughts and scoring were at odds with lots of the final places  :- )<br/> <br/>This is a really nice shot that grows on you the more you look at it. It has a wonderful depth to the picture both in terms of literal DoF and in terms of seeing all that is in there and what is going on - the life and movement - hustle and bustle of the picture.<br/> <br/>Very good - as always . .</td>', 'Surely an underrated shot . . Barring the winner it seems my thoughts and scoring were at odds with lots of the final places  :- ) This is a really nice shot that grows on you the more you look at it. It has a wonderful depth to the picture both in terms of literal DoF and in terms of seeing all that is in there and what is going on - the life and movement - hustle and bustle of the picture. Very good - as always . .', '2008-02-04 15:03:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457616, 638705, 62249, '<td valign="top">Aw, I think this one deserved to do better than it did. And perhaps in a different challenge, one not focused on birds, it would have. For what it''s worth, I like this shot.</td>', 'Aw, I think this one deserved to do better than it did. And perhaps in a different challenge, one not focused on birds, it would have. For what it''s worth, I like this shot.', '2008-02-04 15:04:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457619, 637814, 44877, '<td valign="top">OMG Deb - this is yours! I got the biggest kick out of this photo - just love it to pieces. I figured it wouldn''t score well, because really interesting photos rarely do. But you sure had my 9 for this gem. Just a few days ago I was driving down the road thinking about this very photo and it made me laugh again. I''m going to fav it.</td>', 'OMG Deb - this is yours! I got the biggest kick out of this photo - just love it to pieces. I figured it wouldn''t score well, because really interesting photos rarely do. But you sure had my 9 for this gem. Just a few days ago I was driving down the road thinking about this very photo and it made me laugh again. I''m going to fav it.', '2008-02-04 15:05:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457632, 638274, 68586, '<td valign="top">Ayee !! another underated shot in this challenge . .<br/> <br/>This is such a good shot, and tells so much more of a story than just something sitting looking back at you (like I would have taken :- ))<br/> <br/>This does what a picture should - it tells a story and connects with the viewer.<br/> <br/>Although I have to admit it didn''t seem to connect with that many in this case . . I can only hope some of them come back and take another look at leisure.<br/> <br/>p.s. The title you used was perfect . . I wouldn''t have said the same for ''Bird Butt''  :- )</td>', 'Ayee !! another underated shot in this challenge . . This is such a good shot, and tells so much more of a story than just something sitting looking back at you (like I would have taken :- )) This does what a picture should - it tells a story and connects with the viewer. Although I have to admit it didn''t seem to connect with that many in this case . . I can only hope some of them come back and take another look at leisure. p.s. The title you used was perfect . . I wouldn''t have said the same for ''Bird Butt''  :- )', '2008-02-04 15:09:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457639, 638054, 68586, '<td valign="top">Judi - what are you doing back here ??<br/> <br/>Stop messing about will you and go back up to the front of the class  :- )</td>', 'Judi - what are you doing back here ?? Stop messing about will you and go back up to the front of the class  :- )', '2008-02-04 15:11:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4457652, 638986, 68586, '<td valign="top">Sheesh . .<br/> <br/>Did it meet the challenge ? Clearly not. <br/> <br/>Is it a good phot ? Clearly yes.<br/> <br/>36 1''s ? Well I guess those were DNMC''s . .<br/> <br/>But the 2''s 3''s and 4''s ? What were they about ?<br/> <br/>Technically a great shot, and a title that did enough for me to slide it into the challenge :- )</td>', 'Sheesh . . Did it meet the challenge ? Clearly not.  Is it a good phot ? Clearly yes. 36 1''s ? Well I guess those were DNMC''s . . But the 2''s 3''s and 4''s ? What were they about ? Technically a great shot, and a title that did enough for me to slide it into the challenge :- )', '2008-02-04 15:18:36.000000', NULL, 0),
