(4460235, 638777, 58785, '<td valign="top">Heheheh.... *MA MA*... *MA MA*<br/> <br/>hehehehe</td>', 'Heheheh.... *MA MA*... *MA MA* hehehehe', '2008-02-05 13:08:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4460283, 638957, 67152, '<td valign="top">Cynthia - I think this entry is really close!  I think the details on the bird are really pretty solid- especially as the bird is looking at you but is not dead straight on.  <br/> <br/>For areas that I think could be modified to score better (if that is what you are after).<br/> <br/>1.  Water color choice - The extreme blue color makes this a bit too unnatural compared to the good colors of the bird itself.  Toning back the hue and saturation adjustment just a bit really would have made this seem more real.<br/> <br/>2.  The crop seems a bit tight in the vertical direction.  The length of the photo and the negative space on both sides of the duck is right on the money, but the vertical direction seems far too closed to me as a viewer.<br/> <br/>3.  The somewhat harsh light on the duck seems to limit the amount of details in the feathers we might be able to get.<br/> <br/>Here is a quick edit with a bit of adjustment in the blue hue and a drop in saturation, and a cloning in of some more of the water to provide more room for the duck to breathe.   <br/> <br/>I don''t know if it is better, but it was the first couple things I thought of to bring up the score for the DPC viewers.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=642811" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/65000-69999/67152/120/642811.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/65000-69999/67152/120/642811.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/65000-69999/67152/120/642811.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Oh, and by backing off on the darkness of the blue - we can see more details in the ripples around the duck!<br/> <br/><i>p.s.  I hope you don''t mind me taking a crack at an edit!</i><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-05 13:36:41.</i></td>', 'Cynthia - I think this entry is really close!  I think the details on the bird are really pretty solid- especially as the bird is looking at you but is not dead straight on.   For areas that I think could be modified to score better (if that is what you are after). 1.  Water color choice - The extreme blue color makes this a bit too unnatural compared to the good colors of the bird itself.  Toning back the hue and saturation adjustment just a bit really would have made this seem more real. 2.  The crop seems a bit tight in the vertical direction.  The length of the photo and the negative space on both sides of the duck is right on the money, but the vertical direction seems far too closed to me as a viewer. 3.  The somewhat harsh light on the duck seems to limit the amount of details in the feathers we might be able to get. Here is a quick edit with a bit of adjustment in the blue hue and a drop in saturation, and a cloning in of some more of the water to provide more room for the duck to breathe.    I don''t know if it is better, but it was the first couple things I thought of to bring up the score for the DPC viewers.   Oh, and by backing off on the darkness of the blue - we can see more details in the ripples around the duck! p.s.  I hope you don''t mind me taking a crack at an edit!', '2008-02-05 13:29:49.000000', '2008-02-05 13:36:41.000000', 0),
